%description:
Test connection setup with a forking listener (B): the timeout of the
connection setup in SYN_RCVD closes the forked connection. The tester
deletes all of B's SYN-ACKs. At t=75 s both connections time out; the forked
connection closes, and B keeps one connection, its listener. Before, the
forked connection returned to LISTEN, and B had two listeners.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
record-vector-results = false
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib

cmdenv-express-mode=false

*.testing=true
cmdenv-log-prefix="[%c]: "

*.srv_app.fork=true
*.tcptester.script="b1 delete;b2 delete;b3 delete;b4 delete;b5 delete;b6 delete;b7 delete;b8 delete;b9 delete;b10 delete"

include ../../lib/defaults.ini

%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "^\[testing\]\|finishing with" test.out > test_1.out || true
%contains: test_1.out
[testing]: srv_tcp: SYN_RCVD --> CLOSED  (on TIMEOUT_CONN_ESTAB)
[]: TcpTestNet1.cli_tcp: finishing with 0 connections open.
[]: TcpTestNet1.srv_tcp: finishing with 1 connections open.
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
%postrun-command: grep "undisposed object:" test.out > test_undisposed.out || true
%not-contains: test_undisposed.out
undisposed object: (
%#--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
